        "problem": "The function $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-x+4, & x<1, \\\\ 2x-3, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}.",
        "worked_solution": "By the additive property of the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-3}^{1}(-x+4)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{1}^{4}(2x-3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+4x){|}_{-3}^{1}+({x}^{2}-3x){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =[\\,-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}+4\\cdot 1-(-\\frac{(-3)^{2}}{2}+4(-3))]+\\,[{4}^{2}-3\\cdot 4-({1}^{2}-3\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{2}+4-(-\\frac{9}{2}-12)]+[16-12-(1-3)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{7}{2}-(-\\frac{33}{2})]+6 \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{2}+6 \\\\  & =20+6 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
